WEBVTT

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:09.340
From Hollywood, the Jack Benny program.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.540
Wilson, you finished playing already?

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:29.890
Only playing Dine Hall.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:33.120
Oh, Sidney, will you see that these clubs are put in my car, please?

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:33.680
Yes, sir.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:35.960
Hiya, Don.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:37.150
Oh, hi.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:38.760
Why'd you play so early?

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.820
Well, confidentially, every time I come into the club later in the day,

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.400
I run into Jack Benny, and I wind up having to play with him.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:46.280
I know what you mean.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.900
Jack is such a poor sport, always griping.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.720
Nobody in the club wants to play with him.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.130
But after all, Don, he is your boss.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:54.960
Well, that's the worst part of it.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:57.120
Every time I beat him, he cuts my salary.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.980
My golf sport and my standard of living are going down to...

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:29.390
together. Oh, hi, Dundee. Oh, hi, fellas. Say you were looking for a fourth. How about joining us? Oh, no, no, I just finished. Well, come on, go around again. Oh, no, no, I'm too tired, but thanks anyway, fellas. Well, okay. Well, let's go upstairs and see if we can find somebody to play with us. Hi, fellas. Sorry, Jack, all filled up. What's with those guys? Nobody shakes hands anymore. Everybody runs.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:32.600
Hi, Don.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:33.640
Hello, Jack.

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:34.660
You got a game?

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.060
Oh, I just finished.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:37.940
Well, why do you play so early?

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.720
Well, I, uh, I, uh...

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.080
You what? You what?

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:49.030
Well, I, uh, I like to play early in the morning when the grass is damp and it's chilly and foggy and cold.

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:54.950
Sorry I can't play with you, Jack.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:59.760
That's all right. I'm, uh, I'm playing with the pro anyway, Eric Mondi, you know.

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:01.510
Gary, she was playing with you.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:02.350
Yes, sir.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:05.860
Boom.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.280
That would have been a good one.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:09.490
Oh, Sidney.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:10.010
Yes, sir?

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:13.580
Sidney, will you put some new spikes in my other pair of golf shoes, please?

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:14.860
Well, I'll be happy to, Mr. Wilson.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.400
I got them here in the locker. I'll get them for you.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:20.660
Let's see.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.120
It must be in here someplace.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:25.710
Well, why don't you take some of those things out?

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:27.860
Well, that's a good idea.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.340
They're in the Butter Keeper.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:05.640
Hard to believe that he plays golf just to lose weight.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.880
I'll fix these for you right away, Mr. Wilson.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.180
Thanks, Sidney. Oh, and look, if you have time,

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:13.720
will you defrost my locker, please?

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.120
Jack, I'm sorry I can't play with you today.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:21.740
That's all right. I love playing with Eric Monty.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.650
You know, when you play with a pro, it makes you play better yourself.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:26.440
Well, there's Eric now.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:33.460
Eric, Eric.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:34.780
Sorry, I'm all filled up.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.880
Well, of course you're filled up.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.420
You're playing with me.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.340
Oh, yes.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:43.060
Gee, Eric, I'm all excited about our game today.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:44.180
You're excited?

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:46.450
I didn't sleep all night.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:49.670
Oh, thank you.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:50.600
Thank you.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.080
Do you think there'll be many on the course today?

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:54.630
I don't think so.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.280
Lately, everybody's been playing early in the morning

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:59.960
when the grass is damp and it's chilly and foggy.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:08.780
I thought the idea of the game was to get some sunshine.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:10.220
It used to be.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:12.080
What?

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:18.290
Uh, nothing. Uh, uh, Jack, when you're dressed, I'll meet you on the first tee.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:21.270
Okay. Try and get another couple so we can have a foursome, will ya?

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.920
I'll try. I'll try.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:36.770
What's going on, Artie Stebbins? You just made a hole-in-one.

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:38.990
I sure did. Dropped it in with a three-iron.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.530
Come on, fellas. Come on into the bar. The drinks are on me.

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:48.610
Gee, that... that Artie is a nice guy.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:51.970
Just because he made a hole-in-one, he's buying drinks for everybody.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:55.370
Oh, Jack, being a nice guy has nothing to do with it.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.380
It's customary. When you make a hole-in-one,

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:58.980
you buy drinks for everybody in the club.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:01.410
For all the members?

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:04.490
Gee, it's so expensive and everything.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:06.730
Gee, it must cost Artie a couple of hundred dollars.

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:08.350
Well, that's the way it works, Jack.

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:09.910
It's an unwritten rule.

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.620
You make all in one, you have to buy the drinks.

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:14.830
Well, then what are we waiting for?

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:16.450
Come on, let's get ours.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.930
Oh, we don't have to go.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:19.810
It's right here.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.560
All right, let me through everybody.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:26.540
Let me through everybody.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:39.840
Oh, bottle?

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:41.160
What's the difference?

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:44.470
I mean, Artie has to buy about 400 drinks.

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:46.290
One bottle isn't going to make any difference.

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:50.850
Mr. Benny, Mr. Benny, Eric Monty is waiting for you on the first tee.

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:51.970
Gee, I'd better hurry.

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:55.070
Hey, Sidney, get me my golf shoes.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:05:59.120
You playing today?

00:05:59.570 --> 00:05:59.850
Yes.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.020
We've only got a twosome.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:01.880
Oh, wonderful.

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:03.280
Do you mind if we join you?

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.680
Everett has to finish Irving.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:05.800
Not at all, fellas.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:06.660
Glad to have you along.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:07.180
Fine.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.060
Who are we playing with?

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:09.140
Jack Benny.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:11.620
Well, maybe some other time.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:17.440
All right, did you get another couple?

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:18.890
Almost.

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:22.830
Well, I might as well tee off, huh?

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:24.070
Yes, go ahead.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:25.200
Yay.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:34.760
Gee, it's a little breezy today.

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:36.980
Might as well get some loft on this.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.260
Tee it up a little higher.

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:46.860
I don't think that's high enough.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:48.120
Enough in this breeze.

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:55.520
Think I ought to tee it any higher?

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:57.360
Higher? It looks like a lollipop now.

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:01.810
Yeah, I guess it's high enough.

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:04.050
Well, here goes.

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.580
I don't know, I don't feel comfortable.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.360
Well, stop rocking.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.420
Well, I'm not doing it purposely.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:19.880
Oh, for heaven's sake, what do you think happened?

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:23.720
You know, when you page me, I change my shoes in such a hurry,

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.320
I put my art supports in upside down.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:29.900
I feel like I'm standing on a camera.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.100
Listen, I'll go and change my shoes.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.180
You go ahead and shoot.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:55.940
That was a good one.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:57.650
I like that one.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:07:59.540
Hey, Mr. Monty.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:03.710
Since this is our guest's day, and you're only playing a twosome,

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:05.770
would you mind if these two gentlemen joined you?

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:06.550
They're from Milwaukee.

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:07.910
No, that's fine with me.

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:10.610
Well, this is Mr. Simpson, Mr. Herbert, Eric Monty.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:11.530
Eric, nice to know you.

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:12.410
Hi, Eric.

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:14.720
And this is Jack Benny.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.040
Jack Benny?

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:17.860
Well, this is a great pleasure.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:18.580
Thank you.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:20.880
Jack Benny, this is great to meet you.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.120
Well, thank you.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:23.620
I hope you don't mind us joining you.

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:26.060
No, no, the more the merrier.

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:29.980
Fellas, play away.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:30.860
Go ahead, Herb.

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:31.560
Oh, Jake, Joe.

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:48.290
Why don't we play for a little money, make it interesting?

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:50.470
Eric and I'll stand you two.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.580
All right, Mr. Benny, if you'd like to have a little bet,

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:53.500
what did you have in mind?

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:55.260
One, two, five?

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.120
How about making it 10?

00:08:59.010 --> 00:08:59.330
Jack!

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:04.180
It's all right with us. Ten a hole.

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:08.840
No, no, let's say ten for the whole game, you know.

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:10.980
Well, that sounds a little better to me.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:13.060
Okay, ten dollars for the match.

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:15.230
No, ten cents.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:21.430
Well, Jack, you certainly didn't make it interesting.

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:23.510
Why not?

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:39.300
Very good.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:40.720
Fine shot.

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:52.150
Say, Mr. Simpson, do you mind if I make a suggestion?

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:53.030
Not at all.

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:55.450
You've got your feet just a little bit too far apart.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:57.170
Put them just a little bit closer together.

00:09:57.710 --> 00:09:58.090
Thanks.

00:09:58.460 --> 00:09:59.120
Wait a minute.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:05.600
We're betting against them. Don't try to help them, for heaven's sake.

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:06.560
Wait a minute.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.240
Put your feet where they were.

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:22.170
Right down the middle.

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:23.530
Sir.

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:25.740
Well, I guess I'm next.

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:34.730
I don't want this real high this time.

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:58.010
I told you you had a team too high. Try it again.

00:10:58.750 --> 00:10:59.250
Okay.

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:13.530
Oh, that was much better.

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:14.700
Yeah.

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:23.520
Jack, we have a candy today.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.490
Yeah, here he is.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.320
I was patting again.

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:12.140
Let's see now, we won the first hole, you and Eric won the second, and we have the third, and we took this...

00:12:12.140 --> 00:12:16.260
